# 高频词汇 List07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List07核心词汇

propose /prəˈpəʊz/ v. 提议 The committee proposed a new set of guidelines. 委员会提出了一套新的指导方针。
prospect /ˈprɒspekt/ n. 前景 The prospects for renewable energy are bright. 可再生能源的前景是光明的。
pursue /pəˈsjuː/ v. 追求 She decided to pursue a career in research. 她决定从事研究事业。
radical /ˈrædɪkl/ adj. 激进的；根本的 The situation calls for radical reform. 这种情况需要根本性的改革。
range /reɪindʒ/ n./v. 范围 The study covers a wide range of topics. 该研究涵盖了广泛的主题。
rational /ˈræʃənl/ adj. 理性的 We need a rational approach to solving the problem. 我们需要一种理性的方法来解决问题。
react /riˈækt/ v. 反应 The market reacted negatively to the news. 市场对这一消息反应消极。
recover /rɪˈkʌvə(r)/ v. 恢复 The economy recovered after the recession. 经济在衰退后恢复了。
reduce /rɪˈdjuːs/ v. 减少 We must reduce carbon emissions. 我们必须减少碳排放。
reflect /rɪˈflekt/ v. 反映 The data reflects changing consumer preferences. 数据反映了消费者偏好的变化。
reform /rɪˈfɔːm/ v./n. 改革 The education system needs comprehensive reform. 教育系统需要全面改革。
region /ˈriːdʒən/ n. 地区 The region has experienced rapid urbanization. 该地区经历了快速的城市化。
regulate /ˈreɡjuleɪt/ v. 调节；监管 The industry is regulated by government agencies. 该行业由政府机构监管。
reject /rɪˈdʒekt/ v. 拒绝 The proposal was rejected by the majority. 该提案被多数人拒绝。
relate /rɪˈleɪt/ v. 关联 The findings relate to earlier studies. 这些发现与早期研究有关。
release /rɪˈliːs/ v./n. 释放；发布 The company released its annual report. 公司发布了年度报告。
relevant /ˈreləvənt/ adj. 相关的 Only relevant information should be included. 只应包含相关信息。
reliable /rɪˈlaɪəbl/ adj. 可靠的 We need a reliable source of data. 我们需要可靠的数据来源。
reluctant /rɪˈlʌktənt/ adj. 不情愿的 He was reluctant to change his opinion. 他不愿改变自己的看法。
rely /rɪˈlaɪ/ v. 依赖 We cannot rely on a single source of income. 我们不能依赖单一的收入来源。
remove /rɪˈmuːv/ v. 移除 The obstacle was removed from the road. 障碍物从路上被移除了。
require /rɪˈkwaɪə(r)/ v. 需要 The position requires advanced technical skills. 该职位需要高级技术技能。
research /rɪˈsɜːtʃ/ n./v. 研究 Further research is needed to confirm the findings. 需要进一步的研究来确认这些发现。
resolve /rɪˈzɒlv/ v. 解决 The dispute was resolved through mediation. 争端通过调解解决了。
resource /rɪˈsɔːs/ n. 资源 Human resources are the most valuable asset. 人力资源是最宝贵的资产。
respond /rɪˈspɒnd/ v. 回应 The government responded quickly to the crisis. 政府对危机做出了快速反应。
restrict /rɪˈstrɪkt/ v. 限制 Access to the area is restricted. 进入该地区受到限制。
retain /rɪˈteɪn/ v. 保留 The company struggled to retain skilled workers. 公司努力留住熟练工人。
reveal /rɪˈviːl/ v. 揭示 The study revealed surprising results. 该研究揭示了令人惊讶的结果。
revenue /ˈrevənjuː/ n. 收入 The company's revenue increased by 20%. 公司的收入增长了20%。
